        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131">

                <pb facs="0294" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg198"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-02-01"><hi rendition="#italic">February 1,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 136.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Colonel Denby’s dispatch, No.
                    2916 of April 20, 1898, concerning the murder of a Chinese hospital student at
                    Chiang Pei, near Chung-king, in March last, I have the honor to report that the
                    case has been finally settled upon still more favorable terms than those agreed
                    upon by Colonel Denby.</p>
                <p>I inclose a copy of the conditions agreed upon, and a dispatch from Consul
                    Smithers with information that all the conditions had been faithfully executed.
                    Also a copy of the proclamation of the Taotai issued in accordance with the
                    terms of the agreement.</p>
                <p>The settlement has been considerably delayed, first by a long series of literary
                    examinations, making arrests and punishments unwise for a time, and then by the
                    absence of the missionaries for the summer, and because of the long time
                    necessary to communicate with the consul, and the difficulty of adjusting the
                    details to the satisfaction of all taking part therein. However, it is now
                    finished and apparently satisfactory to all.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>





